    id: 'Book-1-2', title: 'Want Out of Jail? First You Have to Take a Fast Food Job', short: 'The cost of getting out', author: 'Anna Wolfe & Michelle Liu', year: 2020, genre: 'Investigative reporting', theme: 'Justice & accessibility', motif: 'ledger', color: '#815641',
    question: 'What happens when release depends on money instead of a fixed date?',
    summary: 'Wolfe and Liu investigate Mississippi’s restitution centers through Annita Husband’s experience and wider records. Residents work at low-paying jobs while confinement and other costs can add to what they owe. Unclear accounts and release conditions make it difficult to know when punishment will end. The authors contrast official descriptions of a community transition program with residents’ restrictions and distress. Husband’s escape, later prison term and remaining debt give the investigation a narrative thread. Aggregate earnings data and interviews show that her experience connects to a broader system whose effects extend well beyond a single missed payment.',
